// Hello, world: a program printing a line through `Console`, an effect the
// host provides. Its handler is the runtime at the run target, writing each
// line to standard output; a test runs the same program under a handler that
// keeps the lines. `gandr run hello.gandr` prints `hello, world!` and exits 0.

/// The entry: it prints its greeting and returns the unit, which exits 0.
@[ runs("hello, world!\nunit") ]
def main() -> -F [Console] Unit {
  Console.print("hello, world!")
}

main()
